cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ChorusKD: Black-Box Knowledge Distillation via Diverse Sampling, Consistency Voting, Capability-Matched Scheduling, and Ranking-Based DPO"
abstract: >-
  A black-box knowledge distillation framework for the setting where the teacher
  exposes only generated text through a paid API: no logits, no hidden states.
  ChorusKD treats distillation as a closed-loop controller over multiple rounds,
  combining temperature-spread sampling, character-level consistency voting as a
  label-free quality proxy, student-loss-based difficulty scheduling with
  hysteresis, listwise teacher ranking turned into DPO preference pairs, and
  zero-cost keyword domain routing across multiple teachers.
